<title>BULGARIA: Bulgarian coal mine explosion injures nine.</title>
<headline>Bulgarian coal mine explosion injures nine.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>A methane gas explosion injured nine miners at Bulgaria's Bobov Dol coal mine on Monday, officials said.</p>
<p>&quot;One has a broken leg, four are in a serious condition,&quot; the national energy committee said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said four others suffered less serious burns from the explosion, which occurred when a ventilator was switched on after a power cut.</p>
<p>Five miners have been killed this year in accidents at the mine, which is 70 km (42 miles) west of Sofia.</p>
</text>
